wasmtime 37.0.3: the warnings it gives with the engine's features and toolchain, fixed.

Built from a path (engine/crates, for wasmtime-37.0.3-shared-memory-fault.patch) wasmtime is a
local package, whose lints cargo does not cap as it does a registry package's: its warnings show,
and they are kept on, so that a warning in what we patch shows too. There were 23, none a fault:

  runtime/vm/libcalls.rs:119, 20 of them (unused variable: `value_contref`, `delta`, `addr`, …):
    the libcall macro's stand-in for a libcall of a feature that is compiled out (#[cfg(not(…))],
    unreachable!()) uses vmctx only (`let _ = vmctx;`); the engine leaves features out
    (stack switching, the component model, …), so their parameters were unused. Those stand-ins
    alone allow unused_variables (#[cfg_attr(not(…), allow(…))]: the macro cannot repeat the
    parameters inside the feature's optional group, so `let _ = (vmctx, …)` does not expand).
  runtime/vm/sys/unix/signals.rs:52, 114, 218 (direct cast of function item into an integer):
    `trap_handler as usize` and alike, which a lint newer than wasmtime 37's MSRV (1.87) flags with
    the pinned 1.98.1; cast through `*const ()` as it suggests. The value is the same.

--- a/src/runtime/vm/libcalls.rs
+++ b/src/runtime/vm/libcalls.rs
@@ -114,6 +114,9 @@
                 // implementation and automatically perform `catch_unwind` along
                 // with conversion of the return value in the face of traps.
                 #[allow(improper_ctypes_definitions, reason = "__m128i known not FFI-safe")]
+                // A libcall of a feature compiled out stands in with unreachable!(): its
+                // parameters go unused there, and only there.
+                $(#[cfg_attr(not($attr), allow(unused_variables))])?
                 pub unsafe extern "C" fn $name(
                     vmctx: NonNull<VMContext>,
                     $( $pname : libcall!(@ty $param), )*
--- a/src/runtime/vm/sys/unix/signals.rs
+++ b/src/runtime/vm/sys/unix/signals.rs
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
             // crash while handling the signal, and fall through to the
             // Breakpad handler by testing handlingSegFault.
             handler.sa_flags = libc::SA_SIGINFO | libc::SA_NODEFER | libc::SA_ONSTACK;
-            handler.sa_sigaction = trap_handler as usize;
+            handler.sa_sigaction = trap_handler as *const () as usize;
             unsafe {
                 libc::sigemptyset(&mut handler.sa_mask);
                 if libc::sigaction(signal, &handler, slot) != 0 {
@@ -111,7 +111,7 @@
                 // signal handler state and don't know how to remove ourselves
                 // from the signal handling state. Inform the user of this and
                 // abort the process.
-                if prev.sa_sigaction != trap_handler as usize {
+                if prev.sa_sigaction != trap_handler as *const () as usize {
                     eprintln!(
                         "
 Wasmtime's signal handler was not the last signal handler to be installed
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@
                 unsafe { wasmtime_longjmp(jmp_buf) }
             }
             unsafe {
-                set_pc(context, wasmtime_longjmp_shim as usize, jmp_buf as usize);
+                set_pc(context, wasmtime_longjmp_shim as *const () as usize, jmp_buf as usize);
             }
             return true;
         }
